---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { Header, Footer } from '../components/ui';
import { getLanguages, slugFor } from '../lib/content';
import '../styles/business.css';
const languages = getLanguages();
---
<Base title="Minimal-pair listening activities for language teachers | MinimalPairs" description="Use short listening activities, phonemic examples and explicit dialect notes in your language lessons. No student account is needed for the starter collection.">
  <Header /><main class="editorial-wrap"><p class="eyebrow">FOR LANGUAGE TEACHERS</p><h1>Give listening a specific focus.</h1><p class="editorial-lede">A short sound contrast can make an abstract pronunciation explanation easier to hear. Use these activities as a listening warm-up or a focused follow-up to a lesson.</p><section><h2>A simple lesson sequence</h2><ol><li><strong>Introduce the contrast.</strong> Explain which sound feature matters and which dialect is being practiced. Keep spelling out of the first listening attempt.</li><li><strong>Listen before answering.</strong> Students hear references A and B, then a different word X. They decide which reference shares X’s target sound, with text hidden by default.</li><li><strong>Compare and revisit.</strong> Replay the references and X. Reveal words and meanings afterward if useful. Return later with unfamiliar words and voices to check whether the distinction transfers.</li></ol><p>Repeated-item practice accuracy is not a proficiency assessment.</p></section><section><h2>Choose your language</h2><div class="editorial-link-grid">{languages.map(language => <a href={`/${slugFor(language)}`}><strong>{language.name}</strong><span>{language.dialect} →</span></a>)}</div></section><section><h2>Open an activity without a class account.</h2><p>Share an exercise link or open it on a classroom screen. Students can practice without providing an email. Their guest history stays on their own device.</p><a class="button button-dark" href="/practice">Explore the exercises →</a></section></main><Footer />
</Base>
